@startuml
title Proposed / Future | independent OVN domains with GoBGP Type-2
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFD
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #64748B

rectangle "Domain A | independent OVN control plane\nNBDB / northd / SBDB A\nNode-Agent A + GoBGP A\novn-controller / OVS A + endpoint A" as a
rectangle "Domain B | independent OVN control plane\nNBDB / northd / SBDB B\nNode-Agent B + GoBGP B\novn-controller / OVS B + endpoint B" as b

a -[#2563EB,dashed]- b : BGP EVPN Type-2 control
a -[#15803D,dashed]- b : proposed external VXLAN packet path

legend bottom
  Proposed topology; no independent-domain end-to-end validation.
  Blue: BGP Type-2 control | Green: workload packets
  No shared OVN NBDB / SBDB is assumed.
  Importer owns only its exact Linux FDB / neighbor state.
  ovn-controller observes it and programs OVS.
  Exact route and imported-state ownership stay local.
  Shared-OVN results do not validate this inter-domain packet path.
endlegend
@enduml
